WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.167 --> 00:00:02.752
I bet you never thought

00:00:02.752 --> 00:00:04.004
you'd see a Lamborghini

00:00:04.004 --> 00:00:06.339
going off-road
in the Mojave Desert.

00:00:07.298 --> 00:00:09.843 position:59%
Well, the Lamborghini Huracán Sterrato

00:00:09.843 --> 00:00:11.511
is out to change that.

00:00:16.391 --> 00:00:18.685
Here we are out in
Joshua Tree, California.

00:00:18.685 --> 00:00:21.187 position:63%
It's about an hour east of Palm Springs,

00:00:21.187 --> 00:00:22.731
so we're way out in
the middle of nowhere

00:00:22.731 --> 00:00:25.191
with a Lamborghini,
if you can imagine it.

00:00:25.191 --> 00:00:26.818
The Lamborghini Huracán Sterrato.

00:00:26.818 --> 00:00:28.695
This is the off-road version

00:00:28.695 --> 00:00:30.280
and it's also the end of an era

00:00:30.280 --> 00:00:33.825
because it's the last V10
internal combustion engine

00:00:33.825 --> 00:00:35.744
that Lamborghini will ever make.

00:00:35.744 --> 00:00:37.120
So it's kind of a big deal.

00:00:37.120 --> 00:00:39.080
It's also been a long time coming.

00:00:39.080 --> 00:00:41.624 position:66%
We saw early versions of this car in 2019,

00:00:41.624 --> 00:00:43.001
it's finally here.

00:00:43.001 --> 00:00:46.796
The base price is $273,000.

00:00:46.796 --> 00:00:48.465
I hear it's going to
be really fun to drive.

00:00:48.465 --> 00:00:50.467
I can't wait to go try it.

00:01:07.859 --> 00:01:09.527
Have you ever been on this track?

00:01:09.527 --> 00:01:11.404
No, never. This is completely new.

00:01:12.655 --> 00:01:15.325
With brutalist undertones
and a low seating position

00:01:15.325 --> 00:01:19.412
this Sterrato comes with a
601-horsepower, V-10 engine

00:01:19.412 --> 00:01:23.041
and 413 lb-ft of torque.

00:01:23.041 --> 00:01:24.709
It has all-wheel drive

00:01:24.709 --> 00:01:28.129 position:75%
a 0-60 miles per hour sprint time of 3.4 seconds

00:01:28.129 --> 00:01:31.800 position:59%
and a top speed of 161 miles per hour.

00:01:33.718 --> 00:01:35.970
Now, don't feel bad
if you're a little skeptical

00:01:35.970 --> 00:01:39.682
about this $273,000 supercar.

00:01:39.682 --> 00:01:40.934
I was too.

00:01:40.934 --> 00:01:44.729
Lamborghini has no record
of success in off-road rallies

00:01:44.729 --> 00:01:47.315
in the 60 years since
the brand roared to life.

00:01:47.315 --> 00:01:51.194
But that hasn't stopped the brand
from jumping into the off-road mix.

00:01:51.194 --> 00:01:54.739
I spoke with Lamborghini
head of design Mitja Borkert

00:01:54.739 --> 00:01:56.658 position:61%
about what makes the Sterrato different

00:01:56.658 --> 00:01:57.575
from a normal Huracán.

00:01:59.619 --> 00:02:03.164
Our design DNA is about
the single center silhouette.

00:02:03.164 --> 00:02:04.833
You can always tell a Lamborghini

00:02:04.833 --> 00:02:06.626 position:66%
in front of you with the inclined windows.

00:02:07.544 --> 00:02:09.462
Every car of Lamborghini,

00:02:09.462 --> 00:02:12.048
that's my mission,
has to have this character.

00:02:12.799 --> 00:02:15.385
So for the customer it
is clear what is the car.

00:02:15.385 --> 00:02:17.387
So we took it in a higher position.

00:02:17.387 --> 00:02:19.931 position:56%
We have a slightly longer wheelbase.

00:02:19.931 --> 00:02:21.057
We have bigger wheels.

00:02:21.057 --> 00:02:24.227
More important,
of course, the rallycross wheels.

00:02:24.227 --> 00:02:26.855
We added the cladding,
we kept it quite rough

00:02:26.855 --> 00:02:29.691
because we wanted to give this
tough and rugged feeling.

00:02:30.984 --> 00:02:32.402
It's the everyday super sports car,

00:02:32.402 --> 00:02:33.319
you don't need to care,

00:02:33.319 --> 00:02:34.320
you just drive.

00:02:34.320 --> 00:02:38.283
It's the car that is your
partner for any adventure.

00:02:38.908 --> 00:02:40.869
It's unbelievable
what the car can do.

00:02:40.869 --> 00:02:41.327
Yeah.

00:02:41.327 --> 00:02:41.870
Unbelievable.

00:02:44.706 --> 00:02:47.709
I was driving this thing harder
than I drove the Rivian truck,

00:02:47.709 --> 00:02:49.586
rougher than I drove a Porsche 911

00:02:49.586 --> 00:02:51.421
or a Land Rover in the sand dunes.

00:02:51.421 --> 00:02:54.507
I came out of the car
grinning from ear to ear.

00:02:54.507 --> 00:02:55.049
Wow.

00:02:58.386 --> 00:03:01.931 position:80%
But now I wanted to see how it did on the pavement.

00:03:01.931 --> 00:03:04.434
Passing by the Joshua trees
and desert dry hills

00:03:04.434 --> 00:03:06.144
the Sterrato just cruises.

00:03:06.144 --> 00:03:07.353
Man, it's pretty fun.

00:03:07.353 --> 00:03:13.151 position:59%
It's pretty great to go directly
from the dirt onto an asphalt surface.

00:03:13.151 --> 00:03:15.612
And I have to say,
driving in Joshua Tree

00:03:15.612 --> 00:03:18.448
is the perfect way to explore

00:03:18.448 --> 00:03:19.824
both sides of the car.

00:03:22.535 --> 00:03:25.663
The Huracán Sterrato
has three main driving modes,

00:03:25.663 --> 00:03:27.081
Strada, Sport and Rally.

00:03:27.081 --> 00:03:30.501
Now, Rally is the one that we used
when we were going off-road.

00:03:30.501 --> 00:03:32.545 position:56%
That's where everything super loose,

00:03:32.545 --> 00:03:34.756
very minimal stability control,

00:03:34.756 --> 00:03:36.925 position:78%
basically just the anti-lock braking system is on.

00:03:36.925 --> 00:03:38.593
Now we're in sport mode,

00:03:38.593 --> 00:03:40.220
which is a more generalized mode.

00:03:40.220 --> 00:03:43.139 position:59%
It's perfect for driving some of these
back roads in Joshua Tree.

00:03:44.307 --> 00:03:46.309 position:59%
Lamborghini is going to be introducing

00:03:46.309 --> 00:03:47.143
more and more hybrids.

00:03:47.143 --> 00:03:48.728
We've already seen the Revuelto

00:03:48.728 --> 00:03:50.438
and we will soon see

00:03:50.438 --> 00:03:52.774 position:56%
hybrid versions of the Urus as well.

00:03:52.774 --> 00:03:57.070
So this really is, in a way,
the end of an era for Lamborghini.

00:03:57.070 --> 00:04:00.949 position:73%
The last V10 with an internal combustion engine

00:04:00.949 --> 00:04:03.034
and it's pretty cool
to be able to drive it.

00:04:05.161 --> 00:04:06.955
My take, the Huracán Sterrato

00:04:06.955 --> 00:04:07.997
is a joyful ode to the

00:04:07.997 --> 00:04:10.541
contrarian nature of Lamborghini.

00:04:10.541 --> 00:04:14.295
Lamborghini is making
just 1,499 of them,

00:04:14.295 --> 00:04:15.964
deliveries begin this summer.

